PATCH 476: FUN_0000_077e -- the engine's ARCTANGENT rebuilt at 16-bit register widths (it hung on a
zero-length vector and returned wrong angles everywhere else).

asm 0x77e-0x845 (SS=DS=DGROUP=0x1c00): octant folding into bp, a shift-and-add normalise of cx:bx against
dx:ax, a bytewise+bitwise scale until ch's bit7 is set, the `cmp dx,cx / cmc / sbb bx,bx` divide guard,
`div cx`, the DGROUP arctan table at 0x2448 (interpolated via `mul cl`/`add ax,0x80`/`dec ch` unless the
ss:0x2040 no-interpolation flag is set) and finally the three octant bits rotated into the result by
`shr bp,1; rcr ax,1` x3 + `adc ax,0`.  Ghidra rendered all of it over 32-bit C locals, so every 16-bit
wrap became a bit-31 test and the `add bx,ax` / `adc cx,dx` zero-exit became unreachable: a vector whose
DX is 0 only after 16-bit truncation (the caller passed 0x10000) spun the normalise loop forever.  That
froze the AZER1 self-play inside a single c0e5 object walk at t=16988 once patches 462/475 let the AI
reach a coincident object pair -- and until now every bearing the engine computed came out of the same
32-bit-wrapped code.  Reconstructed 1:1; the callers (0731/0578/054c/059a/3425) are unchanged.
